/// known-gap: interp takes no digits argument to round
/// `:round(x, n)` keeps n digits after the point and gives a float; a
/// negative n rounds to tens, hundreds, ... and gives a whole number. A
/// whole number with n >= 0 stays as it is. `:round(x)` is unchanged.
say(:round(3.14159, 2))
say(:round(2.5, 0))
say(:round(-1.005, 1))
say(:round(1234.5, -2))
say(:round(7, 2))
say(:round(3.7))
say(:round(25%, 1))
